Subject: [PATCH 02214/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1 (CLOSE
 THE CROSS-DOMAIN SELECTION MOAT; rebuild the underpowered exp4305) -- a
 domain router + per-domain set-encoder that generalizes selection to a
 HELD-OUT DOMAIN, rebuilt with the flagged SOTA + more power. .398 (exp4305)
 reported a POSITIVE point estimate (cross_domain_delta +0.231) but CI95
 [-0.115,0.538] INCLUDED 0 (underpowered, NOT refuted);
 label_ablation_robust=true (no domain-label leak);
 GAP-CROSS-DOMAIN-FAMILY-INVARIANT-SELECTION-4305 logged. The .398 SOTA
 ingestion (exp4309) + the .399 sweep flagged the precise upgrades: (1)
 replace the nearest-centroid router with an IR3DE LINEAR domain-expert router
 (ridge regression over normalized selector features, leave-one-domain-out;
 arXiv:2606.06098); (2) add CASCAL GENERATED-DATA synthetic-task pretraining
 (train-only synthetic selector tasks from domain descriptions, query-only
 routers, no target labels; arXiv:2601.09692) for more router training signal;
 (3) add ContextPRM domain-AGNOSTIC step-COHERENCE features (verify the
 logical connection, not the domain fact; arXiv:2509.24460) as the
 domain-invariant discriminator; (4) MORE held-out tasks (>=~24) for power.
 Keep the LABEL-ABLATION anti-leak arm + the non-degenerate guards
 (vote@1>0.05, oracle<1.0, delta<0.95) so the adversarial_verify
 DEGENERATE_SEPARATION check does not fire. Domains: ARC families + ARC-GEN
 generators (reuse exp4291's non-degenerate pool) + FoVer-step/math (NOT code
 -- exp4319 owns code-execution). Emit cross_domain_selection_holds BARE bool
 := (held-out-domain delta>0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND non-degenerate guards AND
 label_ablation_robust). verifier_is_oracle=false. A held-out-domain win
 escapes the math/ARC domain bound (the strongest selection result yet); a
 powered collapse is a genuine, decision-grade scope boundary. HARD-CAP to the
 window; an honest partial (>=3 domains, >=1 held-out, >=~16 held-out tasks)
 is fine.

